## Security and configuration keys (all milestones)

These are environment-variable names, not values. Never put real values in this
file, Swagger, source code, screenshots, or Git.

| Key | Used by | Purpose | Safe example |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `SECRET_KEY` | Backend and business logic | Signs and validates JWT bearer tokens | `long-random-value` |
| `ALGORITHM` | Backend and business logic | JWT signing algorithm | `HS256` |
| `ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES` | Backend and business logic | Login-token lifetime | `30` |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Backend, AI/CV and business logic | Database connection string | `sqlite:///./app.db` |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | Backend | Comma-separated permitted frontend origins | `https://app.example.com` |
| `NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_URL` | Notification gateway | Internal notification endpoint base URL | `http://backend:8000/notifications` |
| `ENV` | Backend | Selects `.env.<ENV>` configuration file | `production` |
| `VITE_BACKEND_URL` | Frontend build | Public backend base URL | `https://api.example.com` |
| `VITE_AI_API_URL` | Frontend build | Public AI-service base URL | `https://ai.example.com` |

**Authentication headers**

```http
Authorization: Bearer <access_token_from_/auth/login>
```

Use a bearer token for every protected user or service action. No static API
key is accepted by the active platform routes.

