## Complete endpoint index by milestone

The URLs below are the routes registered by the single current FastAPI application.
Business logic is available only under `/business`, so every route uses the same
configured database and authentication policy.

### Canonical naming and roles

`Learner` is the canonical name for the person who learns and practises;
`student` is a deprecated synonym. `Lesson` and `lesson_id` are the canonical
public content terms; `course` and `course_id` are legacy storage aliases.
New clients must use `/lessons`, `learner_id`, and `lesson_id`. The platform has
exactly four roles: `Learner`, `Instructor`, `Accessibility Trainer`, and
`Admin`. Instructors see their assigned learners; Accessibility Trainers see
only their separately assigned learners' analytics; Admins manage users,
lessons, and assignments.

